  "question": {
    "text": "Two blocks <math><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> of masses <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> are kept on the table as shown in figure. The coefficients of friction between <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> is <math><mn>0.2</mn></math> and between <math><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> and the surface of the table is also <math><mn>0.2</mn><mo>.</mo></math> The maximum force <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math> that can be applied on <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> horizontally, so that the block <math><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> does not slide over the block <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> is : [Take <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></math> ]<br /><img src=\"assets\\qt0122_bcf935a4084e.png\" style=\"width: 280px; height: 159px;\" />"
  },
